</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">Q1.66.05<a name=\"ipccc-Q1.4666.4605\"> </a></td><td>- due to extreme cold</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">Q1.66.06<a name=\"ipccc-Q1.4666.4606\"> </a></td><td>- due to fire</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">Q1.66.07<a name=\"ipccc-Q1.4666.4607\"> </a></td><td>- due to infiltrate from intravascular catheter</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">Q1.66.08<a name=\"ipccc-Q1.4666.4608\"> </a></td><td>- due to infiltrate from intra-arterial catheter</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">Q1.66.09<a name=\"ipccc-Q1.4666.4609\"> </a></td><td>- due to infiltrate from intravenous catheter</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">Q1.66.10<a name=\"ipccc-Q1.4666.4610\"> </a></td><td>- due to skin preparation solution</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">Q1.66.11<a name=\"ipccc-Q1.4666.4611\"> </a></td><td>- medication</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">Q1.66.20<a name=\"ipccc-Q1.4666.4620\"> </a></td><td>- grade 1: discoloration of intact skin not affected by light finger pressure (non blanching erythema)</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">Q1.66.21<a name=\"ipccc-Q1.4666.4621\"> </a></td><td>- grade 2: partial-thickness skin loss or damage involving epidermis and-or dermis (superficial ulcer presenting as abrasion or blister or shallow crater)</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">Q1.66.22<a name=\"ipccc-Q1.4666.4622\"> </a></td><td>- grade 3: full thickness skin loss with subcutaneous tissue damage (not extending to underlying fascia)</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">Q1.66.23<a name=\"ipccc-Q1.4666.4623\"> </a></td><td>- grade 4: full thickness skin loss with extensive destruction and necrosis extending to underlying fascia</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">Q1.66.30<a name=\"ipccc-Q1.4666.4630\"> </a></td><td>- due to patient immobility or being bedridden</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">Q1.66.31<a name=\"ipc